WEBVTT

00:20:30.371 --> 00:20:33.579
So I think that speaks to some really
interesting questions about communication

00:20:33.579 --> 00:20:35.996
and coordination. You know,

00:20:36.079 --> 00:20:38.621
certainly since Darwin wrote
about facial expressions,

00:20:39.246 --> 00:20:43.413
we've been curious about the universality
versus specificity of of

00:20:43.413 --> 00:20:45.538
different kinds of facial
signals of emotion.

00:20:46.538 --> 00:20:49.704
This is this has been an incredibly
heated debate in psychology over

00:20:49.704 --> 00:20:53.371
the last few years. Which facial
expressions of emotion do you think are

00:20:53.371 --> 00:20:55.454
most universal from your
studies of chimps

00:20:55.454 --> 00:21:01.329
and which ones seem to be idiosyncratic
to either individuals or to groups